From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Sable settings page in one list

Settings > Sable becomes one list of the Sable settings, after
BlackBerry 10's settings list (owner pick from the JL10 review): Sable
Setup, Display (sizes and accent), Home screen (Sable Start's Edit
Home), Home style, Hub (connected apps), Attention, Lock screen,
Keyboard and Diagnostics (Sable Tools). Each row has an icon, a title
and a one-line summary and opens an existing page; a row whose app is
missing is hidden and left out of search. The homepage row is now
"Sable" and opens this page instead of Sable Setup directly.
---
 res/values/strings_sable_settings.xml         | 26 ++++++--
 res/xml/sable_settings.xml                    | 65 +++++++++++++++++--
 res/xml/top_level_settings.xml                |  2 +-
 .../android/settings/sable/SableLinks.java    | 35 +++++++++-
 .../settings/sable/SableSettingsFragment.java |  8 +--
 .../TopLevelSablePreferenceController.java    | 25 ++-----
 6 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

